Z||000004||Mach10||06-03-2001||09:33 PM||||Erk. Without pulling it off and looking at the casting, I can't really say. Uh, I THINK that one's a Series-1. Correct? I can try and find out.<P>Shiner:  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Yeah, good 'ole "Lucas, prince of Darkness"<BR>A few quirks:<BR>-Lucas Positive Ground system (fun at parties when 'jumping' cars)<BR>-Lucas 2-position, 3-way switch: Off, dim, Flickering<p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 06-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tweek||06-03-2001||10:05 PM||||Yep, Its definatly a series 1,  They went to series 2 midway thru '73. Easiest way to identify that change is because of Fed. law here in the US they had to raise the front bumper, It ended up above the parking light, making the grill significatly shorter.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||06-03-2001||10:30 PM||||I own a S-2 XJ6L FROM ENGLAND! Yep! Right-hand steering! Lovely racing green. At least where it isn't primered  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">.<BR>It's a project-on-hold until we figure out what to do with the lemon-flavored transmission.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tweek||06-04-2001||09:32 AM||||Well, one route you could go is GM's th-350. Its a common tranny conversion for the xj's. Im pretty sure mine is good, but after driving the car 10 feet and realizing the brake didnt work I didnt do it again. I dont know if youve looked around much on there, but I highly recommend taking a look at <A HREF="http://www.jag-lovers.org" TARGET=_blank>www.jag-lovers.org</A>  One of the best jag resources on the internet. Also their mailing list is just as knowlegable and civil as this forum..  anywooo   Im going up to see my folks today, Im gonna take more pictures while im there...||||reg||1
Z||000008||Mach10||06-05-2001||07:31 PM||||*Smach*<BR>SACRILIGE!<P>Tweek: It's a little bit of a tricky swap. In addition, you have to worry about the t-350 having TOTALLY the wrong gearset  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> The t-700 is a much better solution.<P>Actually, we're more interested in having OEM equipment in it. Keeps the resale value up, which is more or less what we're looking for. It's a shame though. It's a great cruiser.<BR>||||reg||1
